    "body": "## Summary\n- build the real final API and web production images in a dedicated security workflow\n- scan both images with Trivy on pull requests, master pushes, a weekly schedule and manual dispatch\n- fail closed on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL OS or library vulnerabilities\n- ignore vulnerabilities with no available vendor fix for the merge-blocking gate, while continuing to refresh the scan weekly\n- generate a CycloneDX SBOM for each production image and retain both as GitHub Actions artifacts for 30 days\n- keep the workflow secret-free and read-only with respect to repository contents\n\n## Why\nDependency audits and CodeQL cover source/dependency risk, but they do not prove that the final JRE/nginx container layers are free of known fixable critical vulnerabilities. Scanning the built runtime images closes that gap. The same image inspection also produces reproducible SBOM artifacts for release/security investigations.\n\n## Merge gate\nMerge only after both image scan jobs and the repository's normal relevant checks are green on the exact PR head, with master unchanged and the branch 0 commits behind.",
